{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and Frankie Valli feel like natural next choices because they connect with my classic rock compilations and mid-'60s hits listening.",
    "Neil Diamond and Bread fit the mellow, melodic side of my interest in Simon & Garfunkel and singer-songwriter recordings."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour and 25 lean toward contemporary ballads, while I want familiar older hits right now.",
    "Number One Hits and The Greatest Hits Collection do not identify an artist, so I cannot tell whether their songs match the music I enjoy.",
    "To Be Loved and Santana have some appeal, but that does not make them immediate choices: older hits collections appeal more than the vocal connection today, and Eagles is my stronger classic rock choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits title alone seems to count too much; whose songs are included matters more to me than the compilation label.",
    "My interest in vocal albums seems to have been stretched too far toward contemporary ballads, despite my stronger interest in older songs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated connection to familiar '60s-era songs and classic rock matters more to my current choices than a broad connection to popular music.",
    "I distinguish between music that generally appeals to me and what I would choose today; a plausible connection to Cheek to Cheek is weaker than my current desire for nostalgic hits."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in melodic classic hits, but stretched that interest too broadly to contemporary vocals and unidentified compilations."
}"}
